#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Standblatt user has My training: club users open it from the start page or the user menu, shooters without a club sign up themselves. Email address, password, language, second factor and deleting the account live on the [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account) page, which **Account** in the sidebar or **Settings → Account** opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sign up"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Create an account** on the login page. You need your name, your email address and a password of at least 10 characters. You are logged in right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Sign-up](../images/screenshots/my-signup.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt sends you a link to confirm your email address. Until you confirm it, a note on the Today page reminds you; **Send again** sends a new link. The link is valid for seven days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Forgot your password? See [Forgotten password](../user-guide/login-language.md#password). Logged in, you change the password under [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Accounts created by a club admin log in with their user name instead of an email; they can add an email address under **Settings → Email**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Profile and competition results {#competitions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Settings → Profile** you can enter your **birthday** and **license number**. With both, Standblatt finds your results from events run with Standblatt by any club, for example the club championship. They show up in the **Log** under *Your competition results* once the club has closed the event, that is, once the ranking is final. Each result carries your **rank** in the programme (for example *Rank 12 of 87*). Choose the discipline and tap **Add**, or **Add all**. Added results become competition sessions with their series and keep the rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Own disciplines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "Six disciplines are built in: air pistol and air rifle 10 m, pistol 25 m and 50 m, rifle 50 m and 300 m. For anything else, e.g. a field programme, add **Own discipline** in the settings with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "the usual number of series and shots per series,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "whole or decimal (up to 10.9) scoring and the highest value of a shot,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "optionally a target face for tapping hits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons {#weapons}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shoot more than one gun, e.g. two air pistols? Add them under **Settings → Weapons** with a name of your choice; the calibre does not matter. Choose the weapon when you save a session and [Progress](progress.md#weapons-compared) compares them. Renaming a weapon keeps its sessions. Deleting it keeps the sessions too, they just have no weapon any more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API tokens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Want to import sessions from another app or analyse your log with your own script? Create a token in your account with the preset **Training app**; see [API tokens](../user-guide/login-language.md#api-tokens)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the app"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt is a web app that can be installed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Android / Chrome**: Settings → **Install**, or *Add to home screen* in the browser menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "**iPhone**: Share → *Add to Home Screen*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "Installed, it starts full screen. A long press on the icon offers *Start training*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Your data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Export all sessions (CSV)** downloads every series of every session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account** removes the account with all sessions, goals and settings after you enter your password. Accounts that belong to a club must first be removed from the club by its admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My training"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is a personal shooting diary. Every shooter can use it, whether or not their club runs events with Standblatt. It answers one question: **does my training work?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"grid\" markdown>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Today on a phone](../images/screenshots/my-today.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress of a discipline](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Logging takes seconds.** After a session you tap the + button, type the series totals on the number pad and save. Standblatt moves on to the next series by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**As detailed as you like.** Log only the series totals, every shot value, or tap every hit on the target. You can switch per series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Feedback right away.** After saving you see how the session ranks among your sessions of the same length and how it compares with your last 30 days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Progress you can read.** Trend, personal best, goal, series curve, shot values, the size and centre of your group, what your tags tell you and how your weapons compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Competitions come for free.** Results from events run with Standblatt are found by your license number and birthday once the club closes the event, and added with one tap, rank included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Works at the range.** Install it on the home screen. Without signal, sessions are kept on the phone and uploaded later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Your data stays yours.** Export everything as CSV at any time and delete your account whenever you want."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Page | What it is for |\n|---|---|\n| **Today** | start a session, this week's activity, your recent trend and sessions |\n| **Log** | every session, filtered by discipline and kind, competition results waiting to be added |\n| **Progress** | the analysis of one discipline, see [Progress explained](progress.md) |\n| **Settings** | profile (name, birthday and license number for the competition match), own disciplines, weapons, app, export; **Account** for email, password, language, second factor and deleting the account |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a phone the pages are in the bar at the bottom, with the + button in the middle. On a larger screen they are in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Access and price"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is free for every user of the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Club staff accounts can use My training too: open **My training** in the user menu of the club sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap the **+** button, or a discipline under **Start training** on the Today page. The session opens full screen with your last discipline already selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Series totals on the number pad](../images/screenshots/my-train-series.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "At the top you see the running total, the number of shots and the average per shot. Below that is a chip for every series. Tap a chip to correct that series, tap **+** to add one, or use **Remove series** for the current one. The minus and plus next to \"10 shots\" change the number of shots of the current series, e.g. for a 5-shot series at 25 m."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Three ways to enter a series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the input for the current series at the top right. You can mix them in one session, e.g. totals for the first four series and every shot for the last two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Series**\n: Type the series total. As soon as no further digit could make the number valid, Standblatt takes it and jumps to the next series. \"9\", \"3\" gives 93 and moves on; a 100 needs \"1\", \"0\", \"0\". With decimal scoring the point is added for you: \"1\", \"0\", \"2\", \"7\" gives 102.7. **Next** takes the number as it is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Shots**\n: Tap the value of every shot. With decimal scoring type two digits, e.g. \"9\", \"7\" for 9.7, or three for a ten, e.g. \"1\", \"0\", \"4\" for 10.4. After the last shot of a series the next series starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Target**\n: Tap where every shot hit. Standblatt computes the value from the target face of the discipline, with decimals if the discipline is scored that way. The magnifier switches between the black and the whole target. This is the only way to get the [group analysis](progress.md#group).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Tapping hits on the target](../images/screenshots/my-train-target.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a computer you can type the digits, **Backspace** and **Enter** on the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Save"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the last series is complete, or when you tap **Finish**, the save sheet opens. Everything in it is optional:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Training or competition**: competitions appear as their own dots in the trend and are compared with your training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Weapon**: which of your [weapons](account.md#weapons) you shot with. A new session starts with the weapon of your last session in the same discipline; tap it again to clear it, or add a new weapon right there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**How did it feel?**: five faces from bad to great."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Tags**: short words for what was special, e.g. *new grip*, *tired*, *new pellets*. Progress compares the sessions with a tag to your average."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**When**, **where**, **notes**. *Where* starts with the place of your last training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![After saving](../images/screenshots/my-result.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "After saving Standblatt tells you right away:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "whether the session is a **new personal best**, or which place it takes among your sessions with the same number of shots;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "how many points per shot it is above or below the average of the **30 days before**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unfinished sessions and offline"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "The session is kept on the device while you type. If you close the browser or the phone locks, it comes back the next time you start a session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If there is no connection when you save, the session is kept on the device and uploaded as soon as you are online again. A note on the Today page shows how many sessions are waiting. A retried upload never creates a session twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Waiting sessions belong to the account that typed them. If your login expired in the meantime, log in again and they are uploaded; another person logging in on the same device does not get them. If the server refuses one, for example because its discipline was deleted, a note shows the reason and you can **Discard** it. Only new sessions can be saved offline; changing a session needs a connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once you opened the app online, it also opens without a connection and shows your last data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changing or deleting a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the session in the **Log** and use the pencil to change it, or the bin to delete it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Progress explained"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Progress** analyses all sessions of one discipline; choose it at the top right. Everything is computed from the sessions in your log, nothing is estimated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Points per shot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Sessions differ in length: a 50-shot match, two series after work, a 40-shot competition. Standblatt compares them by **points per shot**, the total divided by the number of shots. 9.30 per shot is 465 over 50 shots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key figures"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Last 30 days**\n: points per shot over all sessions of the last 30 days. The arrow shows the change against the 30 days before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Personal best**\n: the highest total among sessions with the standard number of shots of the discipline, e.g. 60 for air pistol. Tap it to open the session.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions**\n: number of sessions and shots logged in this discipline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Competition vs. training**\n: points per shot in competitions minus points per shot in training. A negative number means you lose points under pressure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Trend"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every session is a dot, competitions in amber. The line is the moving average of the last five sessions, so a single bad day does not hide the direction. A dashed line shows your goal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the total you want to reach over the standard number of shots, optionally with a date. The bar compares it with your last 30 days and tells you how much is missing per shot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Series curve"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Points per shot of the first, second, third … series over all sessions. It shows whether you need a series to warm up, or lose concentration towards the end. The strongest series is highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shot values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "How often each value occurred, from the sessions where you logged every shot or tapped the hits. Decimal values count towards their whole number, so 9.7 counts as a 9."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group {#group}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the hits you tapped on the target in your last ten sessions with hits:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Group size** is twice the average distance of your hits from their centre, in mm. It is a robust measure of how tight you shoot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Off centre** is the distance of that centre from the middle of the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the centre sits clearly to one side, Standblatt tells you which way to adjust the sight. Check your hold and trigger first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Group on the target](../images/screenshots/my-session.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons compared {#weapons-compared}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "As soon as sessions of a discipline were shot with at least two of your weapons, a table compares them: the points per shot of all their sessions, of the last 30 days and the best total over the full match. The weapon with the highest average is on top. Sessions without a weapon are not part of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Two air pistols compared](../images/screenshots/my-weapons.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap a weapon, or choose it in the weapon list at the top, and every figure on the page (key figures, trend, series curve, shot values and group) only counts the sessions shot with it. *All weapons* shows everything again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What your tags tell you"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid "For every tag used on at least two sessions: the points per shot of those sessions and the difference to your overall average. Sorted from the best to the worst, this is where you find out whether the new grip pays off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Codes and barcodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration code (QR)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lane sheets and control strips carry a QR code with"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "REGCODEAAAA<registration>AAAAL<license or 0>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "for example `REGCODEAAAA42AAAAL100109`. A hand scanner types it into the search field of the dashboard and presses Enter; Standblatt opens the results of that registration. The license part guards against a code from another shooter; a code of another event is refused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme barcode (Interleaved 2 of 5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can have a barcode, printed as Interleaved 2 of 5 next to the programme on the lane sheet (only the digits count, padded to an even number of digits). Electronic scoring systems use it to pick the programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CSV import"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with the permission *Manage master data* import shooters on the **Shooters** page. The file needs a header row; the separator (`;` or `,`) is taken from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "license;firstname;lastname;birthday;postalcode;city;club\n100100;Sandra;Example;1969-06-02;9999;Hilltown;PS Example\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `firstname` | yes | |\n| `lastname` | yes | |\n| `license` | no | also `licensenumber`; purely numeric numbers are padded to six digits |\n| `birthday` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD` or `DD.MM.YYYY` |\n| `postalcode`, `city` | no | |\n| `club` | no | the shooter's club, matched regardless of upper case and spaces |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "One line per shooter and club; a shooter in two clubs appears twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters are matched by license number, or by name and birthday when there is none. Existing shooters are updated, nothing is deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "A file with invalid lines is rejected as a whole, with the list of lines to fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clubs that are not in the club list stop the import before anything is stored: for each one, choose an existing club (similar names are suggested) or a new one, then **Import** again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results {#results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Import CSV** on an event's **Enter results** page reads results (see [Enter results](../user-guide/results-entry.md#import)):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "license;firstname;lastname;birthday;club;programme;s1;s2;m2;s1_1;s1_2;s1_3\n013756;;;;;Championship;96;93;2;;;\n;Max;Muster;1990-02-02;SG Hilltown;Obligatory;;45;;9;10;8\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `license` or `firstname` + `lastname` | yes | the shooter: found by licence, else by name (and `birthday`, if several have the name); created when not found |\n| `birthday` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD` or `DD.MM.YYYY` |\n| `club` | no | must be in the club list (regardless of upper case and spaces); the shooter joins it |\n| `programme` | yes | barcode, name with variant like `Championship (Sport)`, or the name alone |\n| `s1`, `s2`, … | yes | points per series, decimals with `.` or `,` |\n| `m1`, `m2`, … | no | mouches per series |\n| `s1_1`, `s1_2`, … | no | single shots of series 1, for series that record them; the series is their sum |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "A shooter can have results in a programme only once; a line for results that exist already is an error. Programmes with several [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts) take one line per attempt until the shooter has none left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the shooter is registered for the programme without results, the results go into that registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** in the programme menu or on the programme page downloads a programme as `<name>.programme.json`; **Programme file** under *Add from …* imports it into another event or another club. The platform operator uploads the same files to the global programme library.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\n  \"format\": \"standblatt.programme\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"programme\": {\n    \"name\": \"Championship\",\n    \"variant\": \"Sport\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"barcode\": \"700005002334864165956154\",\n    \"countsForClubCompetition\": true,\n    \"showOnRankings\": true,\n    \"series\": [\n      { \"shots\": 10, \"maxPoints\": 100, \"trackMouches\": false, \"name\": \"\" }\n    ],\n    \"prices\": [\n      { \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"price\": 20 }\n    ],\n    \"awards\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Wreath card CHF 10\",\n        \"kind\": \"card\",\n        \"value\": 10,\n        \"limits\": [{ \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"points\": 370 }]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ageCategory` is one of `u10`, `u13`, `u15`, `u17`, `u19`, `u21`, `elite`, `senior`, `veteran`, `senior_veteran`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`kind` is `card` (wreath card, printed) or `natural` (prize in kind)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`showOnRankings` is the *Show on kiosk displays* switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Combinations and special prizes are settings of the programme within an event and are not part of the file; copying programmes from an earlier event keeps them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Competition rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "This page describes the rules exactly as Standblatt implements them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Age category"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "The category follows from *event year − birth year*; see the table in [Concepts](../getting-started/concepts.md#age-categories). Without a birthday a shooter counts as Elite. The category is fixed when the shooter registers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration is refused when:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme does not belong to the event, is chosen twice or is not active, or more attempts are chosen than it allows;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme has no price for the shooter's age category (\"not open to the age category\");"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "two variants of the same programme are chosen;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme takes series from another programme that is not chosen, or the number of picked series does not match;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "the lane is taken by another active registration or is out of service;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "the shooter is already registered for one of the programmes at this event (a shooter shoots each programme once per event unless it allows several [attempts](../user-guide/programmes.md#attempts); another variant in a separate registration is fine)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane can still be used after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:22 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every series must be entered. Points lie between 0 and the series maximum (by default shots × 10), mouches between 0 and the number of shots, and only on series that track mouches. Saving results gives the most valuable award the total reaches; saving them again keeps the chosen award as long as the new total still reaches it, otherwise the most valuable one reached. Once every programme of a registration has results, the registration is completed and its lane becomes free."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combinations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme marked *combinable with* another programme can take series from it: at registration the shooter picks which series (for example series 2 and 3 of a four-series programme for a two-series programme). The picked series are copied in ascending order and renumbered from 1; the combined programme cannot be edited on its own and follows every change of the source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:30 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Awards"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "An award tier is available to an age category only if it has a limit for it. A shooter can choose any tier whose limit the total reaches; the most valuable tier is listed first and given by default when the results are saved. The server checks the choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranking {#ranking}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "All results of a programme are ordered by:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "higher total;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "the series compared from the last one backwards (the better last series wins, then the second-to-last, …);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "more mouches;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "age: among juniors (U10–U21) the younger shooter first, among the others the older shooter first; non-juniors rank before juniors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ranks are consecutive (1, 2, 3, … even on equal results). The same ranking feeds the staff pages, kiosk screens, the ranking PDF and CSV, and special prizes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Club competition {#club-competition}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only programmes marked *counts for the club competition* take part, and only completed results of shooters with a club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "The score of a result is the sum of its first two series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "A club with fewer than 5 participants is listed as *not ranked*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Of *n* participants the best *max(5, ⌊n/2⌋)* are mandatory, the rest are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Result = ⌊(Σ mandatory + 0.02 × Σ optional) / number of mandatory × 1000⌋ / 1000, i.e. truncated to three decimals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ties: more participants first, then the sorted scores compared one by one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club excluded in the settings of the module *Club competition* (usually the host) keeps its place in the list but gets no rank (\"out of competition\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:56
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Special prizes {#special-prizes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can award special prizes to the best ranks of every age category. Three numbers define them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Ranks per category**, e.g. 3;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants per category** in this programme, e.g. 10;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants of the shooter's club** in the same programme, e.g. 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid "Per age category with enough participants, the first shooters in ranking order whose club has enough participants win; shooters whose club has too few are skipped and the next one moves up. Shooters without a club are not eligible unless the club minimum is 0. The report lists both the winners and the skipped shooters with the reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "!!! example \"From the brochure to the settings\"\n    A brochure says: *\"In every category, ranks 1–3 receive a special prize, provided the category has at least 10 participants and the shooter's club at least 4.\"* That is ranks 3, category minimum 10, club minimum 4.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane lists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lanes are written as a list of numbers and ranges: `1, 5, 7-10`. Standblatt prints them compactly, turning runs of three or more into ranges (`1-3, 5, 7, 8`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Money and numbers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Amounts are shown as `CHF 1'234.50`, dates as `dd.mm.yyyy`. On wreath cards the value can be printed in words in the event's language, e.g. *Fünfundzwanzig Franken*, *Septante et un francs*, *Ventitré franchi*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme ranking ranks one programme. A **classification** ranks shooters over several programmes or over several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts) of one programme, e.g. a section championship as the sum of three programmes, or a club championship over the best three attempts of an annual programme. Classifications appear on **Rankings**, on kiosk displays and as a report; they never change results or awards."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a classification {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "With the module *Classifications* switched on (**Configuration** → **Modules**), **New classification** on **Classifications** in the configuration (admins) opens the editor:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Programmes**: every programme that counts, with its **Counting attempts**. With 3, the best three attempts count (or the first or last three, as set by the programme's *Counting attempt*). A shooter's total is the sum of all counted attempts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Count only the best programmes**: with several programmes, only that many with the highest points count, e.g. the best two of three; 0 counts all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Rank only shooters with all counting results**: shooters who are still missing a programme or an attempt are listed below the ranking without a rank. Without it everybody is ranked by what they have."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Tie-break**: equal totals are decided by the ticked criteria in their order; the arrows change it. *Series from the last one backwards* compares all counted series, *More of the highest single shots* needs [single shots](programmes.md) (more tens, then more nines …), *Age* follows the [SSV rule](../reference/rules.md#ranking). The default is the SSV order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Classes**: separate rankings, each for some age categories, e.g. *Juniors* with U17 to U21 and *Elite* with the others. An age category belongs to one class at most; shooters whose category is in no class are not listed. Without classes everybody is in one ranking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Show on kiosk displays**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Event | Programmes | Settings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Section championship | Obligatory, Field match, Section stich | each counting attempt 1, *Rank only shooters with all counting results* |\n| Club championship over the season | annual programme with unlimited attempts | counting attempts 3 |\n| Shooting festival, best two stiche | three stiche | *Count only the best programmes* 2 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/classifications.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Copy for next year** copies the classifications with the programmes. Deleting a programme removes it from the classifications.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "The dashboard is the desk view of an event: who is shooting on which lane, who is waiting, who is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard](../images/screenshots/dashboard.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting**: registrations on a lane, with the time since they started, the buttons **Results**, **Edit** and **Finish**. When the module *Ammunition desk* is on, **Ammo** records that it was handed out and a green *ammo* badge shows it afterwards (see [Helpers](helpers.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Waiting**: registrations without a lane (for example when all lanes are taken). Without [lane assignment](events.md#modules) (or without a range) there are no lanes and no *Shooting*: the list is called **Registered** and offers **Results**, **Edit** and **Finish**; a registration leaves it once its results are complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Completed**: registrations whose programmes all have results, with an *awards to hand out* badge that opens the results dialog for the handout, or *awards handed out* afterwards (see [Results](results.md#handout))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: every lane is *free*, *occupied* (with the shooter), *reserved* (with the reservation and its end) or *out of service*. A reservation shows from its lead time on. An event on several ranges shows one grid per range, and the registration dialog groups the lanes by range; a shooter who moves to another range is finished and registered again there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "The figures at the top count waiting, shooting and completed registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Waiting* and *Completed* show 50 registrations per page; the arrows below the list turn the pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything updates live: a result entered at another computer or a reservation that starts appears without reloading. The dot next to **live** in the header shows the connection; after a network interruption the page catches up by itself. Without a connection a red bar says so; nothing can be saved then, but open dialogs keep what you typed, so you can save again once you are back online."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Search and scan"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Press ++f4++ anywhere on the dashboard to jump into the search field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Search](../images/screenshots/search.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type a **license number** (digits only, leading zeros optional), a **name** (part of first or last name) or **first and last name** in either order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each hit offers **Register for &lt;club&gt;** for every club of the shooter, or **Open registration** if the shooter is currently registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New shooter** creates a shooter and opens the registration right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "A hand scanner reading the [registration code](../reference/codes.md) on a lane sheet or control strip types the code and Enter: the results of that registration open directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finish shooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Finish** ends a registration before all results are in, for example when a shooter gives up or hands in the targets later. The registration moves to *Completed* and its lane becomes free; missing results can still be entered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Events** lists the events of the club in the groups *Today* (between the first and the last shooting day), *Upcoming*, *Past* and *Closed*; roles with the permission *Configure events* create new ones there. Opening an event shows its dashboard and the other pages of the operation in the sidebar; *Change event* at the top of the sidebar returns to the list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Events](../images/screenshots/events.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration and operation {#configuration}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event has two areas. The **operation** is what you work with on the day: *Dashboard*, *Enter results*, *Rankings*, *Statistics* and the pages of switched-on modules such as *Reservations*. **Configuration** at the end of the sidebar (admins only) opens the set-up of the event; the sidebar then lists its pages, and *Back to the event* returns to the operation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Page | What it holds |\n|---|---|\n| **General** | name, days, ranges, organizer and language (see below) |\n| **Modules** | the building blocks the event uses (see below) |\n| **Programmes** | what can be shot (see [Programmes](programmes.md)) |\n| Pages of modules | e.g. **Reservations** (with the online booking), **Classifications**, **Kiosk displays**, **Helper links**, only while the module is on |\n| **Copy & close** | copy for next year, close, reopen and delete |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "The configuration needs the permission *Configure events*, the operation *Run events* (see [Roles](users.md#roles))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Settings {#settings}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**General** holds what every event has:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Setting | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Name, Date, Ranges | the date is the main day; its year sets the age categories (SSV: competition year minus year of birth, the day itself does not matter, which counts for pre-shooting days in December before a January event); tick every range the event is shot on, or none for an event without lanes (see below) |\n| Shooting days | single days with optional shooting times, for pre-shooting days and multi-day events (registrations count on the day they are made); the main day is always one |\n| Period (season) | for events over weeks or months, e.g. the Feldschiessen from the opening of the range until 31 August: first and last day, plus the weekdays with their shooting times; no weekday ticked means every day. Single days, e.g. the official weekend, add to the period or replace its times on that date |\n| Organizer | printed on documents |\n| Language of documents and kiosk | language of PDFs, CSV exports and kiosk screens, independent of each user's interface language |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Modules {#modules}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Not every event needs everything: a shooting festival books lanes and hands out wreath cards, an annual programme only collects results. **Modules** switches the building blocks of the event on and off; what is off disappears from the sidebar, the dashboard, the programme editor, the rankings and the reports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The modules of an event](../images/screenshots/modules.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Module | What it adds |\n|---|---|\n| Lane assignment | shooters are registered on lanes: the lane grid on the dashboard, the lane status on kiosk displays and scorer links (needs a range; see below) |\n| Reservations | lanes reserved for groups and clubs; its page in the configuration switches on the [online booking](online-booking.md), through which clubs ask for lanes with a public link (needs a range) |\n| Lane sheet, Control strip | the documents printed at registration; the control strip can print with a [print form](print-forms.md#builtin) of the club |\n| Ammunition desk | the **Ammo** button on the dashboard and for the ammunition desk (see [Helpers](helpers.md#ammunition)); leave it off where shooters bring their own, e.g. air pistol and air rifle |\n| Attempts | programmes that can be shot several times (see [Programmes](programmes.md#attempts)) |\n| Awards | wreath cards, prizes in kind and cash prizes; its setting *Print the award value on wreath cards* puts the value in figures and words on the card, *Print form of the wreath cards* chooses a [print form](print-forms.md#builtin) of the club |\n| Special prizes | the best ranks of every age category (switches on Awards, see [Programmes](programmes.md#special-prizes)) |\n| Club competition | clubs ranked by their shooters' results; its setting *Club excluded from the club competition* is usually the host club, listed as *out of competition* |\n| Classifications | rankings over several programmes or attempts (see [Classifications](classifications.md)) |\n| Kiosk displays | rankings on screens in the hall (see [Rankings and kiosk](rankings-kiosk.md)) |\n| Helper links | scorers, ammunition desk and results clerk without an account (see [Helpers](helpers.md)) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "When you create an event, choose what kind it is; this only switches modules on:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Kind | Modules |\n|---|---|\n| Shooting festival | Lane assignment, Reservations, Lane sheet, Control strip, Awards, Special prizes, Club competition, Kiosk displays, Helper links |\n| Annual programme or training | Attempts, Classifications |\n| Feldschiessen | Lane assignment, Awards, Club competition, Kiosk displays, Helper links |\n| Club championship | Attempts, Classifications, Kiosk displays |\n| Custom selection | none |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid "A module that holds data stays on: switch off the kiosk only after deleting its kiosk links, the awards only when no programme has award tiers, and so on; the card says why its switch is locked; Reservations stay on while the online booking link is active. A module another one needs (Awards for Special prizes) stays on as long as that one is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooting times also give the online booking its slots, unless the booking sets other hours for a day (see [Online booking](online-booking.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Club modules {#club-modules}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid "Some modules belong to the club rather than to an event. **Club modules** in the club part of the sidebar (permission *Users and club*) switches them on and off:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Module | What it adds |\n|---|---|\n| Print forms | forms for pre-printed sheets and the *Print form* section of every programme (see [Print forms](print-forms.md)) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events without lanes {#no-lanes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event without lanes, e.g. an annual programme or a Feldschiessen whose results come on paper or from the scoring system, either has no range or switches the module *Lane assignment* off. Then there is no lane grid, no reservations and no scorer links; shooters are registered without a lane and their results are entered as usual. With a range but without lane assignment, documents still print on the range's print agent and programmes can still be tied to the range; without a range, documents open as PDF, because print agents belong to a range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy for next year {#copy}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "On **Copy & close** in the configuration, **Copy for next year** creates a new event with the same ranges, organizer, language, settings, modules and all programmes, including prices, awards, combinations and special prizes, and the [classifications](classifications.md); the shooting days and the period move with the date, weekly shooting times stay on their weekdays. Registrations, results and kiosk links are not copied. The dialog suggests the name with the year (and a leading number like *42.*) counted up and the date one year later; adjust both as needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Copy an event](../images/screenshots/copy-event.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:85
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Templates {#templates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event that is set up well can become a **template** of the club: **Save as template** on **Copy & close** stores a copy with its modules, settings, ranges, programmes and classifications, named after the event without its year. Templates are listed under *Templates* below the events; a template opens in its configuration and can be changed like an event, but it takes no registrations. **New event** offers the club's templates below the built-in kinds: choose one, then give the new event its name and date. **Delete** on the template's **Copy & close** removes it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid "![New event with the kinds and a template of the club](../images/screenshots/new-event.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Close {#close}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid "When an event is over and the rankings are checked, **Close** it on **Copy & close** in the configuration. Closing releases the rankings: shooters with a [personal training log](../my-training/account.md#competitions) now find their results of this event, with their rank in the programme, and can add them to their log. Everything stays visible (dashboard, results, rankings, reports, documents), but registrations, results, awards, programmes and settings can no longer be changed. A banner on every page of the event says so. **Reopen** makes it editable again; results that shooters already added to their logs stay there. Copying a closed event for next year works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:97
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete** (on **Copy & close**) removes an event, but only while nobody is registered for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Login and language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Log in with your email address (or user name) and password: you chose the password when you accepted the invitation of your club, or you received it from your club admin or the platform operator. Club accounts are not created by sign-up; only [My training](../my-training/account.md) has its own sign-up. Logged in, you change your password yourself under [Account](#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "After the login you land on the start page with a card for every club you belong to and one for [My training](../my-training/index.md), which every user has; **Account** and **Log out** are below the cards. Without a club membership the start page takes you straight to My training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Start page](../images/screenshots/home.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "A login stays valid for seven days of inactivity and at most 30 days; with **Stay logged in for 90 days** ticked, it lasts 90 days on that device. After too many failed attempts, logins from the same address are blocked for a while."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your account belongs to several clubs, you choose the club after logging in; **Switch club** in the user menu goes back to that choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Forgotten password {#password}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your account has a confirmed email address, use **Forgot your password?** on the login page. You get a link that is valid for one hour. Setting a new password logs you out everywhere. Without a confirmed email address, ask the operator to set a new password in the admin panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account {#account}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Account** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar), on the start page and in My training's sidebar opens your account settings:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Login**: your user name (it cannot be changed) and your email address. **Add** or **Change** asks for your password and sends a confirmation link; until you confirm, the address counts as *not confirmed* and **Send again** sends a new link. A confirmed address lets you reset a forgotten password yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Password**: enter the current and the new password (at least 10 characters). Other devices are logged out, the one you are on stays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Language and theme**: the interface language of your account and light or dark mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Second factor**: see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**API tokens**: see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account**: only for accounts that belong to no club; the training log, goals and settings are deleted for good. Club accounts are removed by the club admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Account](../images/screenshots/account.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API tokens {#api-tokens}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Want to show the rankings on the club website, import sessions from another app or analyse data with your own script? Create a token under **Account → API tokens** with **New token**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "a **name** that tells you later what uses it,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "a **preset** fills in the permissions for a common use: **Rankings for a website**, **Training app** or **Read only**,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "the **clubs** the token may use (none: only your training log),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "the **permissions**: *Read my training log*, *Log and change my training sessions* and, for the chosen clubs, the [permissions of roles](users.md#roles) your own role has there,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "when it **expires**: in 30 or 90 days, in a year, or never."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "The token (`sb_…`) is shown only once; copy it right away. Scripts send it as `Authorization: Bearer sb_…` (or `X-API-Key: sb_…`). It may do what you chose and never more than your role in the club: if you lose a permission or leave the club, the token loses it at once. It never reaches your password, email, account or other tokens. `GET /api/token` tells a script its name, permissions and clubs. A token makes at most 600 requests in five minutes. The list shows when each token was last used; revoking one stops it at once. Developers find the endpoints under `/api/docs`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Second factor {#totp}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "An authenticator app (Google Authenticator, Aegis, 1Password and the like) can protect your login: after the password, Standblatt asks for the six-digit code the app shows. Set it up under [Account](#account): **Set up**, scan the QR code, enter the current code, **Switch on**. **Switch off** asks for your password. Lost the phone? The operator can reset the second factor in the admin panel. The operator can also switch the feature off for the whole server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "The interface is available in English, German, French and Italian. Without a choice, Standblatt follows the browser's language. **Language** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar) sets it for your account on every device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printed documents, CSV exports and kiosk screens do not follow your choice but the language of the event, so that every printout of an event looks the same (see [Events](events.md#settings))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dark mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid "The sun/moon button in the header switches between light and dark mode; the choice is kept in the browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard in dark mode](../images/screenshots/dashboard-dark.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid "The bottom of the sidebar shows the version of the server, which helps when reporting a problem; in My training on a phone it is under **Settings**. When a new version is released, open pages offer **Reload** within a minute and load it on the next page change at the latest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt renders all documents as PDF:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Document | Format | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lane sheet | A5 | at registration, with QR code and programme barcodes |\n| Control strip | label 90 × 29 mm | at registration, stuck on the target card |\n| Result sheet | A5 | when all programmes have results |\n| Wreath card | A6, printed onto pre-printed cards | after choosing a wreath card award |\n| Print form | any size, printed onto pre-printed sheets | for programmes with a [print form](print-forms.md), once the results are in |\n| Ranking | A4 | from the rankings page, as PDF only (not sent to the range's printer) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Print button prints on the range's printer if one is set up and its print agent is online; otherwise the PDF opens in the browser and can be printed from there. On a phone or tablet the PDF goes to the share sheet instead (print, save to files, send), so the app stays open; if the phone asks for another tap first, a note with a **Share** button appears."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up printers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges → Set up the printers** (admins):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Printing](../images/screenshots/printing.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Connect a computer next to the printers: a Windows PC or a Mac with the [Standblatt Print Agent app](#app) by [code](#connect), or a Linux computer such as a Raspberry Pi with the [headless agent](https://github.com/standblatt/print-agent): **Add print agent**, give it a name and copy the token. One computer can serve several ranges, e.g. *Pistol 25 m* and *Pistol 50 m*: connect it to each range (the app with **Connect another range**, the headless agent with both tokens, separated by a comma)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once the agent is online, it reports its printers and the list shows its version and operating system. Choose the printer for each document (*Certificates* are the certificates from the rankings, *Print forms* every other form of the club) and its options: the options the agent reports for that printer (on Linux tray, paper size and media type, plus further `lp` options such as `fit-to-page` in the text field; on Windows tray, paper, two-sided, scaling and colour)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Test page** prints a small page (90 × 29 mm, the size of the control strip) on the printer of that row with the options chosen there, also before saving: club, range, printer, options and the time. A label printer prints it as a label, other printers in the top-left corner of the sheet. It needs an online agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Recent jobs** shows what was printed and whether it worked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "A job that the agent does not confirm within two minutes is retried; after three attempts it fails. **revoke** removes an agent immediately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Standblatt Print Agent app {#app}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "The app is the simple way for a laptop or PC next to the printers: no token and no settings to type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Download it from the [latest release](https://github.com/standblatt/print-agent/releases/latest): `Standblatt-Print-Agent-Setup.exe` for Windows, `standblatt-print-agent-app-darwin-arm64.dmg` for a Mac with Apple silicon (`-amd64.dmg` for an Intel Mac), the `.deb` or `.rpm` for Linux."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install it. The app is not signed yet: Windows asks once, **More info → Run anyway**; on a Mac drag it into *Applications* and open it the first time with a right click → **Open**. On Windows it installs for the current user without admin rights, with a shortcut in the start menu and on the desktop, and starts with Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Click **Connect a range** and confirm the code in Standblatt (see [below](#connect))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The Standblatt Print Agent app](../images/app/print-agent.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "The window shows for each range whether it prints, with its last jobs, and below the printers of the computer, each with a **Test page** that prints on that computer without Standblatt. **Advanced** has *Start with the computer*, the address of Standblatt (change it only for a test server) and removing a range. Closing the window keeps the app running in the system tray: the icon is green when every range prints, red otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "On Windows and on a Mac the app tells when a new version is out; **Update now** installs it and restarts the app. To give up a computer, remove its range under **Advanced**, revoke its agent on **Ranges → Set up the printers** and uninstall the app (on Windows under *Settings → Apps*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting a computer by code {#connect}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "![A code in the app](../images/app/print-agent-code.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "The Standblatt app on a computer next to the printers needs no token: it shows a code such as `K7QD-4MZP` and opens **Connect a print agent** in the browser. There, log in if asked, check the computer named on the page, choose the club and range and the agent's name, and **Connect**. Only members who may manage ranges can connect a computer; a code is valid for ten minutes. The app then connects by itself, and the agent appears under **Ranges → Set up the printers** with its version and operating system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the browser on that computer is not at hand, type the code on **Ranges → Set up the printers** of the range in **Connect by code** instead: the computer is connected to that range under its own name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print forms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A print form puts results onto a pre-printed sheet, e.g. the lane sheets the army supplies for the obligatory programme: the shots are entered at the lane or afterwards, and the sheet is printed instead of filled in by hand. Filling in sheets by hand stays possible; print forms are optional and can be switched off under **Club modules** (see [Club modules](events.md#club-modules))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a form {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Print forms** (admins, in the club part of the sidebar) lists the forms of the club. **New print form** asks for a name, what the form **Prints** (see [Data source](#source)) and a paper size, then opens the editor. It has three columns:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Fields** on the left: everything a form can print, in groups, with an example each and a search. A click adds the field below the lowest element; dragging it onto the sheet puts it where you drop it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Own text* prints fixed text, *QR code* and *Barcode* print their value as a code, *Line* draws a line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Shooter*, *Club and event* and *Result* print one value each, e.g. the name, the total or the points of a series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Single shots* adds a whole row of shot boxes: *Shots of series 1* is one element `{{s1.shot#}}` repeated once per shot, 8 mm apart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **Sheet** in the middle shows the form true to scale over the scan, with made-up values; **Show field names** shows the placeholders instead. Rulers in millimetres run along the top and the left, the zoom goes from 50 to 200 %."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Properties** on the right edit the selected element exactly: its **Value** (placeholders such as `{{shooter.name}}` are filled in when printing), **x** and **y** in millimetres from the top left corner, **Width** and **Height** (a width of 0 lets text run to the right edge), **Font size**, **Bold**, **Italic**, **Wrap text** (the text breaks into lines within the width, each as high as the height) and **Alignment**. **Repeat** prints it several times, moved by **dx** and **dy** each time; `#` in a placeholder counts 1, 2, 3, …. Below, the **Form** sets the name, the size of the sheet, the printer offset and the **Scan of the empty form**: a PNG or JPEG of the whole sheet that appears behind the sheet so the fields can be placed onto the boxes of the form; it is never printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Save** stores the form; a dot on the button shows unsaved changes, and leaving the page with them asks first. With **Save automatically** (on unless you switch it off; the browser remembers it) unsaved changes are stored every minute. **PDF preview** opens the form exactly as the PDF renders it, which can differ slightly from the sheet in the browser.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data source {#source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "What a form **Prints** decides its fields and where it is printed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Prints | Fields | Printed from |\n|---|---|---|\n| Results of a programme | shooter, club, event, series, single shots, total, award and its value | the results of a programme (see [Use a form](#use)) or as the event's wreath card |\n| A registration | shooter, club, event, lane, programmes, passes, QR code of the registration | as the event's control strip |\n| A rank | shooter, club, event, rank, total, ranking, class | certificates from the rankings |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "The source can be changed in the editor under **Form**; fields the new source does not know print nothing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Built-in forms {#builtin}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt prints the wreath card and the control strip with **built-in forms**, listed below the forms of the club. **Copy** turns one into a form of the club that can be changed like any other, e.g. to move the fields onto another pre-printed wreath card or to add the club's logo. An event then chooses it under **Configuration** → **Modules**: *Print form of the wreath cards* in the module *Awards*, *Print form of the control strips* in the module *Control strip*. Without a choice, or when the chosen form is deleted, the built-in form prints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Print forms with the built-in forms and the image library](../images/screenshots/print-forms.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration documents and certificates {#certificates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "A form that prints **A registration** besides the event's control strip, e.g. a participant card or a receipt, appears in the registration with a button of its own name; it prints on the printer of *Print forms*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "A form that prints **A rank** makes certificates: **Certificates** in the header of every ranking and classification on **Rankings** asks for the form, the class of a classification and the ranks (1 to 3 unless changed), then prints one page per ranked shooter, or opens them as one PDF. Certificates go to the printer of *Certificates* under **Ranges → Set up the printers**. The fields of a rank are the rank, the total, the ranking (the programme or classification) and the class; a programme's certificate knows its results too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Certificates from a ranking](../images/screenshots/certificates.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Arrange the elements {#arrange}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Move** an element by dragging it, **resize** it by its corner. The pink dot on the last box of a repeated element drags the spacing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "While moving, the element **snaps** to the edges and centres of the other elements and of the sheet, and a pink guide shows the line; elsewhere it snaps to whole millimetres. Hold Alt to place it freely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Select several** with Shift or Ctrl and a click, or draw a frame around them on the empty sheet. Dragging moves them together; font size, bold and alignment then apply to all of them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **right click** opens the menu: *Duplicate*, *Bring to front*, *Align* (edges, centres, distribute evenly), *Centre on the sheet* and *Delete*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Key | Does |\n|---|---|\n| Arrow keys | move the selection by 0.5 mm, with Shift by 5 mm |\n| Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y | undo / redo |\n| Ctrl+A | select everything |\n| Ctrl+D | duplicate |\n| Delete | delete the selection |\n| Esc | clear the selection |\n| Ctrl+S | save |\n| Ctrl+mouse wheel | zoom |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Images {#images}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid "Logos, letterheads and other pictures come from the club's image library below the list of **Print forms**: **Upload image** adds a PNG or JPEG of at most 2 MB, named after its file. In the editor, the group **Images** of the fields lists them; a click or a drag puts one onto the sheet, 30 mm wide with the image's own proportions. Its properties choose another **Image**, its position and size, and **Keep the aspect ratio** sets the height to match the width again. An image can be repeated like any other element."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid "An image can be deleted only while no form shows it. **Export** puts the images of a form into its file, and **Import** adds them to the library, reusing an image of the same name the club already has."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Calibrate the printer {#calibrate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printers rarely print exactly where they should. Print a sheet with **Test print**, measure how far the values are off and enter it as **Printer offset right** and **Printer offset down** (negative to move left or up). The offset applies to every element; the preview ignores it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use a form {#use}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Configuration** → **Programmes** of the event, open a programme and choose its **Print form** in the section of the same name; this works while shooters are registered. Every completed programme then offers **Print onto form** in the results: at the desk, on the **Enter results** page and on scorer links at the lane (see [Helpers](helpers.md)). With a print agent and a printer chosen for *Print forms* under **Ranges → Set up the printers**, the sheet goes to that printer (e.g. its manual feed), otherwise the PDF opens (see [Printing](printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/print-forms.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** downloads a form as a file, with its images, and **Import** reads it again, e.g. to share a form with another club.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes belong to an event and are managed under **Configuration** → **Programmes** (permission *Configure events*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The programme list](../images/screenshots/setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New programme** opens an empty programme page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme library**: a template of the global library, maintained by the platform operator."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Earlier event**: copies all programmes of another event of the club, including combinations and special prizes. Programmes whose name and variant already exist are skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme file**: imports a [programme file](../reference/programme-file.md) exported from another event or club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The programme page {#page}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "A click on a programme in the list opens its page. It has the sections of the programme, plus a section for each switched-on [module](events.md#modules) that adds to programmes; **Create** or **Save** at the bottom saves them together."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Programme page](../images/screenshots/programme-editor.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Variant**: programmes with the same name are variants of each other; a shooter registers for one of them. The name field suggests the names of the event's programmes, and as soon as the name matches one, the page says that you are creating a variant and warns when the variant name is empty or already taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Barcode**: printed on the lane sheet for electronic scoring (see [Codes](../reference/codes.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Counts for the club competition** and **Show on kiosk displays**: only while the modules *Club competition* and *Kiosk displays* are on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Series**: shots, maximum points, whether mouches are tracked and whether **Single shots** are recorded, per series. With single shots, every shot can be entered and the series is their sum, e.g. to print them onto a form; the series total alone can still be entered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Attempts** (module *Attempts*, see below): how often a shooter may shoot the programme at the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Prices (CHF)**: only the ticked age categories may shoot the programme. With several attempts, a second field per category is the price of every further attempt (*Nachdoppel*); empty means the same price, 0 means the programme is paid once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Awards** (module *Awards*): name, kind (wreath card, prize in kind or cash prize paid out in money), value and the minimum total per age category; leave a category empty where the award is not available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once shooters are registered for a programme, the **series** are fixed so results keep their meaning; the page says so and greys them out. Everything else can still be changed: name, variant, description, barcode, the flags, prices, series names, award names, values and limits. Age categories and awards can be **added** but not removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "The section **Use** of a saved programme is saved at once with every change, also while shooters are registered:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Active**: inactive programmes cannot be chosen for new registrations; existing ones keep them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Combinable with**: the programme whose series this one may take at registration (not for programmes with several attempts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Range** (events on several ranges): the range the programme is shot on, e.g. *Pistol 50 m*; the registration then offers only its lanes and kiosk displays group the rankings by range. *any* leaves it open. Programmes of different ranges need separate registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Print form** (when the club has [print forms](print-forms.md)): the form the results of the programme are printed onto; *none* prints no form."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Special prizes** (module *Special prizes*, see below) follow as a section of their own. **Export** at the top of the page downloads the programme as a file; **Delete** in the programme's menu in the list is only possible while nobody is registered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Attempts {#attempts}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "By default a shooter shoots a programme once per event. **Attempts per shooter** allows more, e.g. 3 for a lucky target with further attempts at a shooting festival, or **Unlimited** for an annual programme shot over the season."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Counting attempt** decides which attempt the ranking, the club competition, special prizes and *My training* count: **The best** (by the ranking rules), **The first** or **The last**. The ranking shows it as *2/3*: the second of three attempts counts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Only the counting attempt receives an award**: off, every attempt can earn its award (a wreath card per further attempt); on, only the counting attempt gets one, and the award moves when a better attempt is shot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "At registration, a programme with several attempts shows a counter: two attempts at once are two result cards, *Attempt 1* and *Attempt 2*. Further attempts can also be added later in a new registration, or by entering another result on **Enter results**, until the shooter has no attempts left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "The number of attempts can be changed while shooters are registered, but not below the attempts a shooter already has. Programmes with several attempts cannot be combined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "The section **Special prizes** on the programme page awards the best ranks of every age category, for example ranks 1–3 in every category with at least 10 participants, counting only shooters whose club has at least 4 participants in this programme. Skipped shooters make room for the next one. The exact rule is in [Competition rules](../reference/rules.md#special-prizes); the winners are in the report *Special prizes* under [Statistics](statistics-reports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Special prizes of a programme](../images/screenshots/special-prizes.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Save special prizes** stores them; ranks 0 turns special prizes off. The settings can be changed at any time, also after the event.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranges"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges** (admins) lists the shooting ranges of the club.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Ranges](../images/screenshots/ranges.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Number of lanes**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Out of service**: lane numbers that cannot be used, e.g. `3, 7`. They show grey on the dashboard and cannot be assigned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Distances**: a hall with 25 m and 50 m lanes is set up as two ranges, e.g. *Pistol 25 m* and *Pistol 50 m*, each with lanes from 1. An event can be shot on both (see [Events](events.md)), a programme can be tied to one of them (see [Programmes](programmes.md)), and one print agent can serve both (see [Printing](printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Set up the printers** opens the printers and print agents of the range (see [Printing](printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "A range with events cannot be deleted. Lane reservations belong to the range and show in all of its events (see [Reservations](reservations.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings and kiosk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Rankings** shows a live ranking per programme, ordered by the [SSV rules](../reference/rules.md#ranking). The first three ranks are highlighted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Rankings](../images/screenshots/rankings.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**PDF** opens the ranking (A4) for printing or sharing, **CSV** downloads it for Excel. Rankings do not go to the range's printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes switched off for kiosk displays are still ranked here and marked *not on kiosk*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Classifications](classifications.md) follow the programmes, one table per class; their **PDF** and **CSV** are the report *Classifications*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Certificates** prints certificates for the best ranks onto a [print form](print-forms.md#certificates) of the club; the button appears once the club has a form that prints a rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Kiosk screens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "A kiosk link shows the rankings of one event on a screen in the hall, without login. Switch on the module *Kiosk displays* under **Configuration** → **Modules**, then create one on **Kiosk displays** in the configuration:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name for the screen (e.g. *Hall 1*), choose **Dark** or **Light** and optionally a language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Create kiosk link**; copy the link. It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the link in a browser on the screen, ideally in full screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Kiosk screen](../images/screenshots/kiosk.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "The kiosk shows only programmes with *Show on kiosk displays* switched on, and the lane status if *Show lane status on the rankings* is on (on the same page)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "The language is the event's language unless the link carries another one (`?language=de`, `fr`, `it`, `en`); the theme comes from `?theme=dark` or `?theme=light`. On an event with several ranges, `?range=<id>` (chosen when creating the link) limits the display to that range: its lanes, its programmes and the programmes without a range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "The screen updates live and reconnects by itself after a network interruption. When a new version of Standblatt is released, it reloads by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately. *last seen* tells when a screen last fetched data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Helpers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Helpers at the event (scorers, the ammunition desk, the results office) work with a **helper link** instead of a login. A helper link opens a reduced desk of one event on any phone or laptop; admins switch on the module *Helper links* under **Configuration** → **Modules**, create the links on **Helper links** in the configuration and revoke them when the event is over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Scorer's helper page on a phone](../images/screenshots/helper-scorer.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:7 ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Roles {#roles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Role | Sees | Can |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Scorer** | the lane grid of their own lanes, the shooters on them | enter results and awards, **Finish** a shooter |\n| **Ammunition desk** | the search box, the waiting list, the shooters on all lanes | mark the ammunition as issued (**Ammo**), assign a lane to a waiting shooter, print the lane sheet |\n| **Results clerk** | the search box, the shooters on all lanes, the completed list | enter results and awards on every lane |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything else stays with the club's users: registering shooters, editing programmes, rankings, statistics, deleting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a link {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name (who gets the link, e.g. *Scorer range A*), choose the role and, for a scorer, the range and the lanes (`1-5, 8`). One scorer usually looks after several lanes; scorers exist only while the event assigns lanes (module *Lane assignment*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Create helper link**; copy the link and send it to the helper (e.g. by messenger). It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "The helper opens the link; it stays valid until it is revoked or the event is deleted. `?language=de` (`fr`, `it`, `en`) overrides the event's language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately; *last seen* tells when it was last used. A scorer who opens a shooter on another lane gets *This lane is not yours*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ammunition {#ammunition}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ammo** on a waiting or shooting registration records the time the ammunition was handed out; the button exists only when the module *Ammunition desk* is on (air pistol and air rifle shooters usually bring their own). The dashboard shows a green *ammo* badge on such registrations, so the desk and the range officer see at a glance who has been served.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registrations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration puts a shooter on a lane with the programmes they shoot. Open it from the dashboard search (**Register for …**)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Registration dialog](../images/screenshots/registration.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pick a free lane in the grid, or leave it empty: the shooter then waits until you assign a lane by editing the registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Occupied and out-of-service lanes cannot be picked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane asks for confirmation before it is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "The programmes of the event with their price for the shooter's age category. Programmes without a price for that category are greyed out (*not for this age category*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Variants** (same programme name) appear as a choice of one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **combinable** programme offers *take N series from …*: tick it and pick exactly N series of the other programme. The other programme is added automatically if it is not chosen yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **total** at the bottom adds up the prices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooter already registered"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the shooter is or was registered at this event before, a notice lists those registrations with their programmes and a link to open them. Programmes already booked are locked (*already registered*, or *no attempts left* for programmes with several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts)); a shooter may still shoot another variant in a separate registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Print lane sheet* and *Print control strip* are ticked by default (they only appear while the modules *Lane sheet* and *Control strip* are on, see [Modules](events.md#modules)): the documents print on the range's printers right after registering, or open as PDF if no printer is set up (see [Printing](printing.md)). [Print forms](print-forms.md#certificates) of the club that print a registration, e.g. a participant card, add a button each.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Editing and deleting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open a registration from the dashboard (**Edit**) or from the results (*Edit registration*) to change the lane or the programmes. Programmes that already have results cannot be removed; changing the picked series of a combination copies the new series. **Delete** removes the registration with its results after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reservations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Reservations** blocks lanes of the event's range for a time, for example for a training or a group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Reservations](../images/screenshots/reservations.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: a list like `5` or `1, 5, 7-10`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**From** and **To**: the time span. Reservations on the same lane may not overlap; back-to-back is fine."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Show as reserved (minutes before)**: lead time from which the lanes show as reserved on the dashboard and kiosk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Reservations belong to the range, so they appear in every event on that range. Reserved lanes can still be assigned to a shooter after a confirmation. The server announces the start and end of reservations by itself, so screens change without reloading."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Requests that external clubs send through [online booking](online-booking.md) are listed above the reservations; once confirmed, they become ordinary reservations named after the club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Online booking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "With **online booking**, external clubs ask for lanes themselves. The organizer puts a link into the invitation; a club picks the time slots it wants, says how many lanes it needs in each and announces its shooters. An admin confirms or declines every request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Switching it on {#setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "The online booking is part of the module *Reservations* (it needs a range): on **Reservations** in the configuration, **Switch on** is all it takes. The page then shows the link with a QR code for the invitation and the slots it offers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Online booking in the configuration](../images/screenshots/booking-setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without changes, every day of the event is open during its shooting times (see [Events](events.md#settings)), or from 08:00 to 17:00 when it has none, in slots of 30 minutes, and requests are accepted until 14 days before the first day. **Adjust** changes this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting from** and **Shooting until**: the hours of every day without shooting times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Break from** and **Break until**: an optional break, e.g. for lunch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Slot length (minutes)**: how long one slot is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes per slot and club**: a limit per request; empty means no limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Deadline**: the last day clubs can ask or change their request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Days with other hours**: one line per day of the event, e.g. Friday 17:00–20:00. The days come from the event and follow it when you add or remove one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New link** replaces the link; the old one stops working. **Switch off** closes the booking; requests and confirmed reservations stay. *Copy for next year* takes the hours along, but not the link and not the deadline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What a club sees {#club}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The link opens a page without login. It shows the event, the deadline and every slot with the lanes still free on each range. Only confirmed reservations count; names of other clubs are never shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The booking page of a club](../images/screenshots/booking-public.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club enters the number of lanes per slot, its name, a contact person, email and phone, and its **Shooters**: last name, first name, birthday and optionally the licence. **Paste list** takes rows copied from Excel (last name, first name, birthday, licence). The shooter list can follow later; programmes are chosen at the range as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "After **Send request**, the club gets a mail with a personal link. Through it, it can check the status, change the request or cancel it until the deadline. Changing the slots of a confirmed request releases its lanes and the request waits for a new confirmation; adding shooters keeps it confirmed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Confirming requests {#confirm}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every admin with an email gets a mail for each new, changed or cancelled request. The requests are listed at the top of **Reservations**; the sidebar shows how many are waiting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Booking requests on the reservations page](../images/screenshots/booking-requests.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** gives each slot free lanes of its range, neighbours where possible, as an ordinary reservation named after the club, and mails the lane numbers to the club. When a slot has too few free lanes, nothing is reserved and the message names the slot; move a reservation or decline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** first asks which **Club** of the master data the request belongs to, because the club typed its name itself: the club with the same name is chosen already, clubs with a similar name are suggested, and *New club* creates it. The request then shows the club it was matched to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** also takes the shooters into the master data, in that club: a shooter is found by licence, else by name and birthday, and created otherwise. Existing shooters are never overwritten, because the list comes from a public form; only a missing birthday or licence is filled in. Shooters added after the confirmation are taken over with **Take over shooters**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Decline** asks for an optional reason, which goes to the club by mail. Lanes the request held are free again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "The reserved lanes are ordinary [reservations](reservations.md): change their lane numbers there if needed. At the event, the shooters are found with the normal search at the registration desk. The report *Lane bookings* under [Statistics and reports](statistics-reports.md) lists every club with its slots, lanes and shooters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the results of a registration with the **Results** button on the dashboard or by scanning the code on the lane sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Results dialog](../images/screenshots/results.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Entering series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "The cursor starts in the first empty series. As soon as another digit would exceed the series maximum, it moves on to the next field, so a sequence like `96 93 97 88` can be typed without the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Series that track mouches have a second field for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Series with single shots show a field per shot under the series; the series becomes their sum. Enter every shot or none: without shots, the series total is typed as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "++enter++ or **Save** stores the programme. Values above the maximum are marked and cannot be saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Saving again replaces the results; the chosen award stays as long as the new total still reaches it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "A combined programme shows which series it takes from its source programme and fills in automatically once the source has results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "When every programme has results, the registration is completed and its lane is free again. **Print result sheet** prints an A5 summary for the shooter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once a programme is complete, the awards the total reaches in the shooter's age category are listed, the most valuable first; of several wreath cards (or several prizes in kind) only the most valuable one reached is offered. Saving the results already gives the most valuable one; picking another one saves it at once. For a wreath card, **Print wreath card** prints the shooter's data onto a pre-printed A6 card; the value is printed only if the event setting *Print the award value on wreath cards* is on (in figures and in words)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Handing out awards {#handout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the shooter collects the wreath cards, prizes and cash at the desk, press **Awards handed out** in the results dialog, which lists the awards of every programme; the *awards to hand out* badge in the *Completed* list of the dashboard opens that dialog. The registration then carries the time of the handout and a green *awards handed out* badge; until then it shows *awards to hand out*. A wrong click is taken back with **Take back** in the results dialog or by clicking the green badge on the dashboard (club members only, not helper links); the same works for the *ammo* badge. The report **Awards to hand out** (see [Statistics and reports](statistics-reports.md)) lists what is still open and the cash to pay out. A results clerk with a [helper link](helpers.md) may mark awards as handed out too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enter results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Results can be entered in three ways; they can be mixed within one event:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the lane** on a tablet or phone, through a scorer link (see [Helpers](helpers.md)): the scorer enters the series, or every shot, of the shooters on their lanes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**At the desk** through the registration and its results (see [Results](results.md)), the way of a shooting festival."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Afterwards** on **Enter results** in the event's sidebar, shooter by shooter, e.g. from paper sheets or the display of the scoring system, or as a file exported from the scoring system. This page describes both."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooter by shooter {#quick}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the **Programme**; it stays chosen for the next shooters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type a licence number or a name into **Shooter** and press ++enter++: the first hit is taken. A barcode scanner works too. **New shooter** adds someone who is not in the master data yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type the series, or the single shots for series that record them (see [Programmes](programmes.md)), and press ++enter++."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "The result is saved at once and the shooter is listed under *Entered now* with a link to the results. If the shooter was registered at the desk for this programme and has no results yet, the results go into that registration; otherwise a registration without a lane is created, already completed. A shooter can have results in a programme only once, unless the programme allows several [attempts](programmes.md#attempts): then every further result is a new attempt until none is left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "Awards are chosen as usual: the most valuable award reached is set automatically and can be changed in the results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import from a file {#import}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results-entry.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Import CSV** (admins) on **Enter results** reads a file with one line per shooter and programme, e.g. exported from the scoring system or typed in a spreadsheet; the columns are described under [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md#results). Every line is checked first: with any error nothing is imported, and the dialog lists the lines to fix. Shooters who are not in the master data are created; a club must already be in the club list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooters and clubs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each club keeps its own shooter master data; nothing is shared with other clubs. **Shooters** and **Clubs** are under **Master data** in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Shooters](../images/screenshots/shooters.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Search** works like on the dashboard: license number (leading zeros optional), part of a name, or first and last name in either order. The list shows 50 shooters per page, the club list 50 clubs; the arrows below turn the pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clicking a shooter opens the details: name, license number, birthday, address and the clubs the shooter belongs to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Club** (new shooter, or adding a club in the details) suggests the clubs of the list. A name that matches a club regardless of upper case and spaces is that club. Any other name shows *is not in the club list yet* with similar clubs under *Did you mean*; a new club is only created after **Create new club**, so a typo does not become a second club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Import** (admins) reads a CSV file, see [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters with registrations cannot be deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clubs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Clubs](../images/screenshots/clubs.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Clubs** are the clubs shooters belong to, with their SSV number. They appear in registrations, rankings and the club competition. A shooter can belong to several clubs and registers for one of them. Clubs used by registrations cannot be deleted, and two clubs cannot have the same name regardless of upper case and spaces.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/shooters-clubs.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Merge into…** (admins) cleans up a duplicate, e.g. *S.G. Hiltown* next to *SG Hilltown*: choose the club that stays (clubs with a similar name come first). It keeps its name and gets the shooters, registrations and booking requests of the other one, including those of closed events, so their rankings show the club that stays; the SSV number is taken over when it has none. The other club is deleted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Statistics and reports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Statistics** shows the key figures of the event and offers all reports.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Statistics](../images/screenshots/statistics.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Registrations, completion rate, programmes sold, revenue, awards and their value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Participation and revenue per programme, registrations per age category, awards given."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **club competition** with ranked, out-of-competition and not ranked clubs (rules: [Club competition](../reference/rules.md#club-competition))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every report is available as **PDF** and **CSV** (UTF-8 with BOM, `;` separated, opens directly in Excel). Texts follow the language of the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Report | Content |\n|---|---|\n| Financial report | revenue per programme, awards with their value |\n| Revenue by programme and age category | participants, price and subtotal per programme and category |\n| Awards | every award given, with shooter, club, programme, value and result |\n| Club competition | ranking, out of competition and not ranked clubs |\n| Club participants | participants per club, programme and age category |\n| Special prizes | winners per programme and age category, skipped shooters with the reason (see [Programmes](programmes.md#special-prizes)) |\n| Classifications | every [classification](classifications.md) per class, with the points per programme; parts that do not count are in parentheses |\n| Awards to hand out | awards not yet collected, with shooter, club, programme, kind and value, plus the cash still to pay out (see [Results](results.md#handout)) |\n| Lane bookings | the clubs that asked for lanes through [online booking](online-booking.md), confirmed or still waiting, with contact, slots, lane numbers and announced shooters |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/statistics-reports.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "Below the reports, the ranking of every programme can be downloaded as PDF or CSV."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Users** lists the accounts with access to the club, the open invitations and the roles of the club. It is open to roles with the permission *Users and club*, so at least to admins.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Users](../images/screenshots/users.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Members and invitations {#invitations}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Invite by email**: paste one or many addresses (comma separated or one per line, up to 300) and choose the role. Every address gets a mail with a link valid for seven days; the list under the form says what happened to each address. Mails leave at about four per second, so a large list takes a minute."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Accepting**: the link opens a page that says which club invites with which role. Without an account the person chooses a password and is logged in at once; the email address is the login. Whoever has an account with the address logs in first and then accepts. Only then does the person appear among the members."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Invitations** below the members lists the open and the expired ones: **Send again** mails a new link (the old one stops working), **Withdraw** cancels the invitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add user**: for an account without email, such as a shared account at the range: an existing account is added by its user name; for a new account also enter a password (at least 10 characters)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Role**: choose the role of a member in the list. A club always keeps at least one admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Remove** takes away the access to this club; the account itself stays and keeps its other clubs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "What a member may do depends on the role. The matrix under **Roles** has a column per role and a row per permission; a tick gives the permission at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Roles](../images/screenshots/roles.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Permission | Allows |\n|---|---|\n| **See events and rankings** | events, programmes, rankings and classifications |\n| **Run events** | registrations, results, awards, reservations, documents and printing |\n| **Configure events** | create, configure, copy, close and delete events with programmes, classifications, kiosk and helper links and online booking |\n| **Statistics and reports** | statistics, reports with amounts and ranking CSV files |\n| **See shooters and clubs** | the personal data of the master data |\n| **Edit shooters and clubs** | add and change shooters and clubs |\n| **Manage master data** | import shooters, rename, merge and delete clubs, delete shooters |\n| **Ranges and printers** | ranges, print agents and printer settings |\n| **Print forms** | print forms and images (only while the club module is on) |\n| **Users and club** | users, roles, invitations and club modules |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every club starts with four roles:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Role | Permissions |\n|---|---|\n| **Admin** | all; the column cannot be changed and the role cannot be deleted |\n| **Board** | all but *Ranges and printers* and *Users and club* |\n| **Helper** | see and run events, statistics, see and edit shooters and clubs |\n| **Member** | see events and rankings |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New role** adds a role of your own, which may only see the events until you tick more. The pencil renames a role (an empty name keeps the default name), the bin deletes it once nobody has it any more. The app shows each member only the pages and buttons their role allows: a member without *Run events* opens an event on its rankings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid "Members with *Users and club* but without the admin role stay within their own permissions: they give, change, remove and invite only with roles whose permissions they have themselves, and make or change roles only within them. So only admins make, change or remove admins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/users.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "Accounts are global: deleting an account is done by the platform operator in the admin panel. For a forgotten password see [Forgotten password](login-language.md#password)."
msgstr ""
